        "notes": "Uses a source-built FlashAttention 2 wheel with TORCH_CUDA_ARCH_LIST=10.0; the upstream FA3 wheel used for H200 is Hopper-only. LightX2V renamed this runner: its registry key is `flux2` (was `flux2_dev`), and the old name fails at worker init with `KeyError: 'flux2_dev'` from runner_factory -- after a full server start, so it reads as a startup failure rather than a bad name. The registry is the authority: `python -c \"from lightx2v.models.runners.runner_factory import RUNNER_MODULES; print(sorted(RUNNER_MODULES))\"`. The runner also requires `model_variant`: LightX2V split the old flux2_dev runner into `flux2` + model_variant dev|klein, and an absent variant fails at worker init with `ValueError: Unsupported Flux2 model_variant: None` -- a second layer behind the KeyError, each one only visible after the previous is fixed.",
